    "research": {
      "notes": "## 1. Guidance changes\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal found in the window. The most recent update was the Q1 FY27 report, dated by the 8-K as 2026-09-02, which is before the window. It raised FY27 revenue guidance to $7.975–8.225B and non-GAAP EPS to $9.73–10.03. \nQ2 guidance is revenue of $2.025–2.175B and non-GAAP EPS of $2.54–2.64.\n — 2026-09-02 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000100204726000003/ntap-ex99_1.htm\n- \nQ1 revenue was $2.025B, up 29.9%, and beat the Zacks consensus by 9.9%. Non-GAAP EPS was $2.58, 21.1% above consensus.\n — 2026-09-02 — https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/netapp-q1-beat-raised-guidance-163600631.html\n- \nThe quarter had an extra week worth about $65M of revenue.\n — 2026-09-02 — same URL\n- Evercore ISI said the roughly 17% FY27 growth guide looks conservative, because it implies a sharp second-half slowdown. — 2026-10-07 — https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/why-is-netapp-stock-climbing-today-93CH-4936704\n- \nOne aggregator lists the next earnings date as Dec 1, 2026.\n This is an estimate, not a company confirmation. — date unknown — https://www.chartmill.com/stock/quote/NTAP/analyst-ratings\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- Barclays (Tim Long) downgraded to Equal Weight from Overweight and left its target at $219. \nIt cited the roughly 123% YTD gain.\n \nThe note said it saw no meaningful AI inflection yet.\n Investing.com's text says \"Monday\", but other sources say Oct 14. — 2026-10-14 — https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/why-is-netapp-stock-sliding-today-93CH-4949467 and https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/hpe-dell-ntap-stocks-downgraded-barclays-sees-no-meaningful-ai-inflection/cZxfmk2RBp8\n- Evercore ISI upgraded to Outperform from In Line. \nIt raised its target to $300 from $210.\n — 2026-10-07 — https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/ntap-stock-hits-fresh-record-high-after-evercore-upgrade/cZDvS36RBZ5\n- Goldman Sachs raised its target to $240 from $210 and kept Buy. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.marketscreener.com/news/goldman-sachs-raises-netapp-price-target-to-240-from-210-ce785dd9dd8af62c\n- TD Cowen raised its target to $250 from $200 and kept Buy. — 2026-10-06 — https://rallies.ai/news/netapp-inc-td-cowen-raises-target-price-to-250-from-200-b348a7d89e62ee94\n- Loop Capital raised its target to $260 from $215 and kept Buy. The CNN feed lists the headline on Oct 2. — 2026-10-02 — https://www.cnn.com/markets/stocks/NTAP\n- Wells Fargo kept Equal Weight with a $190 target after INSIGHT. — date unknown — https://www.investing.com/news/analyst-ratings/barclays-downgrades-netapp-stock-rating-on-valuation-concerns-93CH-4948367\n- Morgan Stanley and Citi maintained their ratings. — date unknown (around 2026-09-30) — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9103966/netapp-ntap-shares-rise-following-launch-of-novus-storage-architecture\n- Consensus target figures differ by source. \nOne gives an average of $211.69.\n — date unknown — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hpe-dell-ntap-stocks-downgraded-102255493.html. \nAnother gives $195.79.\n — date unknown — https://www.chartmill.com/stock/quote/NTAP/analyst-ratings\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- Nothing material found in the window.\n- The only case found is NetApp v. Stefansson, the former CTO who joined Vast Data. \nA Florida federal judge dismissed it on forum-selection grounds, saying the dispute belongs in Iceland.\n The order was issued in late January 2026, so it falls outside the window. — 2026-01 (approx.) — https://www.sdxcentral.com/news/former-netapp-cto-wins-dismissal-of-lawsuit-after-vast-data-deal/\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n- No named large-customer win, loss or contract change found in the window.\n- NetApp and Oracle announced a fully managed OCI NetApp Storage Service. \nIt is NetApp's fourth native hyperscaler integration.\n \nGeneral availability is expected within 12 months.\n — 2026-09-29 — https://www.itpro.com/cloud/cloud-computing/netapp-ticks-another-hyperscaler-box-with-oracle-cloud-infrastructure-deal\n- \nQ1 free cash flow fell 35.3% to $401M. Accelerated purchasing by some large customers can make growth and cash conversion less even.\n This is a Zacks view, not a company disclosure. — 2026-09-02 — https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/netapp-q1-beat-raised-guidance-163600631.html\n\n## 5. Insider activity\nAll the sales below are dispositions. I found no open-market purchases.\n- CEO George Kurian sold 37,000 shares at $199.95. \nThe sale was under a 10b5-1 plan adopted 2026-06-15.\n — 2026-09-24 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000119312526405401/ownership.xml\n- Director Deepak Ahuja sold 3,450 shares at $200 under a 10b5-1 plan. — 2026-09-21 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000119312526399472/ownership.xml\n- Director Gerald Held sold 5,757 shares at $212. The filing does not flag a 10b5-1 plan. — 2026-10-01 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000119312526414223/ownership.xml\n- Director Carrie Palin sold 5,000 shares at $216.43. The filing does not flag a 10b5-1 plan. — 2026-10-02 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000119312526415633/ownership.xml\n- Four insiders sold between Sep 21 and Oct 2, which is clustered selling. Kurian and Ahuja also sold on 2026-09-14, one day before the window. — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001002047/000119312526393227/ownership.xml\n- GuruFocus puts insider selling at about $36.0M over three months. This is an aggregator figure. — date unknown — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9123348/ntap-downgraded-by-barclays-rating-changed-to-equalweight\n\n## 6. Product and competitive news\n- NetApp launched Novus at INSIGHT 2026. \nIt is a storage architecture NetApp says scales to 100TBps of throughput for AI factories.\n — 2026-09-30 — https://www.computerweekly.com/news/366651416/NetApp-aims-Novus-storage-at-AI-factory-bottlenecks\n- \nOther INSIGHT",
